    {
        "content": "<p>I noticed several PRs around Mayer Vietoris LES and am wondering if there's any relationship with / reuse from <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Proof.20of.20Homotopy.20Invariance.20of.20Singular.20Homology/near/577398141\">#mathlib4 &gt; Proof of Homotopy Invariance of Singular Homology @ 💬</a></p>\n<p>(Incidentally Mayer Vietoris for sheaf cohomology is in <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/610393-Tau-Ceti/topic/new.20results/near/615888768\">#Tau Ceti &gt; new results @ 💬</a> (3rd item))</p>",
        "id": 618989231,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1787655676
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"224323\">Junyan Xu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/583339-AI-authored-projects/topic/Complex.20structure.20on.20S.5E6/near/618989231\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I noticed several PRs around Mayer Vietoris LES and am wondering if there's any relationship with / reuse from <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Proof.20of.20Homotopy.20Invariance.20of.20Singular.20Homology/near/577398141\">#mathlib4 &gt; Proof of Homotopy Invariance of Singular Homology @ 💬</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><del>To the best of my knowledge there is no relationship with / reuse, but currently investigating just to double check <span aria-label=\"slight smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f642\" role=\"img\" title=\"slight smile\">:slight_smile:</span></del> Based on the agent transcripts, there is no relationship with or reuse:)</p>",
        "id": 618992198,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Lezeau",
        "timestamp": 1787656524
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"779253\">Matteo Cipollina</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/583339-AI-authored-projects/topic/Complex.20structure.20on.20S.5E6/near/618987602\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>just a minor note on #<a href=\"https://github.com/deancureton/sphere-six-complex/pull/38/changes#diff-e0aa042ed7a24a99818099327895653f17ac10ea99c163721a2cbb0556097277R138\">38</a>:  isLocalDiffeomorph_comp is already in mathlib: see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Geometry/Manifold/LocalDiffeomorph.html#IsLocalDiffeomorphAt.comp\">#IsLocalDiffeomorphAt.comp</a> .</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Fixed <a href=\"https://github.com/deancureton/sphere-six-complex/pull/51\">here</a> - thanks for pointing that out!</p>",
        "id": 618992844,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Lezeau",
        "timestamp": 1787656745
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><del>It seems a lot of current PRs are focusing on the 6D smooth Poincare (I don't see the connection precisely but the branches start with codex/theta6), but it is not needed, at least for the final statements you adopted, since you don't fix a smooth structure on S^6. The 6D topological Poincare is needed, but I suggest that you leave it as an axiom (as in <a href=\"https://github.com/deancureton/sphere-six-complex/blob/main/SphereSixComplex/Topology/EstablishedRecognition.lean\">EstablishedRecognition.lean</a>), since proving it probably doubles the size of your repo ... but if you prove it it should be trivial to solve <a href=\"https://lean-lang.org/eval/problems/poincare_high_dim_topological/\">https://lean-lang.org/eval/problems/poincare_high_dim_topological/</a>. </del></p>\n<p><del>In other words, I think item 4 and 9C in the <a href=\"https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCetiRoadmap/pull/279/changes\">roadmap</a> are unnecessary for the current statements.</del></p>",
        "id": 619099238,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1787682670
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh sorry, I see you're not using the Formal Conjectures / PR'd LeanEval <a href=\"#narrow/channel/116395-maths/topic/Distinguish.20Between.20Two.20Constructions.20of.20a.20Complex.20Structure/near/618660714\">statement</a>, and <a href=\"https://github.com/deancureton/sphere-six-complex/blob/9bc7ccefda562e61d3cb3d244b4881f174908ae1/SphereSixComplex/ComplexStructure.lean#L64-L68\">the statement in the repo</a> does require compatibility between the complex structure and the standard real smooth structure, so what I said doesn't apply and smooth Poincare is needed. But I'd still suggest you first leave it as an axiom, as that's probably the least doubtful part of the whole proof ...</p>",
        "id": 619102642,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1787683721
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I was thinking of changing the statement in the repo a little since in it's current form it's a little tricky to read.<br>\nPerhaps we could have both? (but target the FC/lean eval statement first)</p>",
