    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110038\">Kevin Buzzard</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/583339-AI-authored-projects/topic/Complex.20structure.20on.20S.5E6/near/619595331\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"224323\">Junyan Xu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/583339-AI-authored-projects/topic/Complex.20structure.20on.20S.5E6/near/619594913\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Why does the AI like to put unnecessary <code>letI</code> like <a href=\"https://github.com/plby/HopfProblem/blob/9ac8a456b526527837d7082ff775213ca8bc9809/Challenge.lean#L44\">this</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Because we do it in mathlib by accident and they train on mathlib.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It is a bit curious that it's in the statement though, since the version in <code>formal-conjectures</code> that they link to does not do this.</p>",
        "id": 619597706,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1787849460
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That might be because last month mathlib merged a linter <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41657\">#41657</a> which stopped people from doing this, but probably the models were trained on a version of mathlib before this was merged, and perhaps the formal conjectures people switched this linter on.</p>",
        "id": 619598174,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1787849590
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh wait though, the linter would probably not catch this, the link above is indeed a pretty random use of <code>letI</code></p>",
        "id": 619598384,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1787849650
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh I think it does prove 6D topological Poincare, assuming the manifold is smooth to start with (as did Smale), by producing a Morse function with two critical points:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MorseCancel</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nonempty_homeomorph_of_homotopySixSphere</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FiniteDimensional</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ChartedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsManifold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝓘</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">T2Space</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CompactSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hdim</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">finrank</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SixSphere</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₜ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SixSphere</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(it's even more general than the LeanEval statement in that E is not fixed to <code>EuclideanSpace</code>)<br>\n(If the manifold is not assumed smooth, we need later work of Newman / Connell.)</p>",
        "id": 619600426,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1787850138
    },
